  "solution": {
    "text": "The general term is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>T</mtext><mrow><mtext>r</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>r</mtext><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mtext>r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mn>3</mn><mfrac><mtext>r</mtext><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msup></math><br />This is rational if <math><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is even and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is a multiple of <math><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0,10</mn></math><br />So, the sum of the rational terms is<br /><math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn></math>"
  }
